        "t1": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>Livermore projects: pools, vineyard views and new tracts</strong></p><p>Livermore sits at the east end of the Tri-Valley, with the Altamont hills behind it. Vineyards line Tesla Road and Vineyard Avenue in South Livermore. Homes on that side of town look over rows of vines toward the hills. A view deck there is wasted behind a picket guard. A frameless glass deck railing, each panel in two spigots with no posts, keeps the vineyard in sight from the table.</p><p>North and east of downtown, Springtown and the newer subdivisions have backyard pools, two-story homes with balconies and open stairs that need a guard. Pleasanton, Dublin and San Ramon customers order the same parts. Typical Livermore projects are a 60\" glass pool fence with a gate, 48\" balcony and deck railings, and custom stair glass for remodels.</p>"
          }
        },
        "t2": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>Heat, wind and the California code in Livermore</strong></p><p>Livermore summers are hot and dry, with afternoons often in the 90s and a wind that funnels through the Altamont Pass. Tempered glass does not fade or warp in that heat, and the 2205 stainless hardware carries a 10-year no-rust promise. There is no salt air this far inland, so cleaning is a hose and a squeegee after the dust settles.</p><p>The California code sets 42\" as the minimum guard height even for houses. A pool enclosure must be 60\", with gaps under 4\" and the gate latch at least 60\" above ground. The City of Livermore building division applies the 2022 Title 24 codes; vineyard parcels outside the city limits go through Alameda County instead. Check with the right office before you order, and read the <a href=\"/pages/california-building-standards-code-for-glass-railings\">California code page</a> for the summary.</p>"
          }
        },
        "t3": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>Delivery to Livermore and installing it yourself</strong></p><p>Orders are processed in 2–3 business days. The crate then travels 5–10 business days by freight carrier to Livermore, with liftgate delivery at the curb or driveway. The price at checkout is final: no duties, tariffs or hidden fees, even though the crate crosses from Canada. Orders over 3,000 USD ship free. Check the crate when it arrives and report any damage within 3 days, before installation; we replace or refund the item at no cost. Custom sizes, including stair glass, take 2–3 business days to process and 2–3 weeks to ship.</p><p>The system is designed for DIY installation, and most standard installations take about 4 hours with the <a href=\"/pages/glass-railing-installation-guide\">installation guide</a> and videos. Spigots fix to wood or concrete with screws sold separately. On a pool deck the top-mount spigot bolts to the slab; on a raised wood deck the side-mount spigot bolts to the fascia.</p>"
          }
        }
